00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:02,397
lasting peace.

266
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:04,657
I didn't have near enough time.

267
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:07,640
Eneru dethroned me before
I could solidify the

268
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:09,090
A treaty.

269
00:17:09,173 --> 00:17:10,003
Wasted efforts.

270
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:12,440
I'm sorry for failing my people.

271
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:13,800
Stop that.

272
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:16,020
You have nothing to apologize for.

273
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:23,400
A legend is passed down through the
generations in Skypiea about its beginnings.

274
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:30,640
It is said that the day the Upper
Yard, the Sacred Grounds, was created,

275
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:35,237
the voice of the island sung forth a
beautiful song that echoed through the skies.

276
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:38,777
It was after that moment
that the tragedy between

277
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:41,740
the people of the sky
and the Shandians began.

278
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,160
As if on cue.

279
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:49,934
And so the legend says when we next
hear the singing voice of the island,

280
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:53,160
this war will finally come to an end.

281
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:56,260
The voice.

282
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:57,780
That's right.

283
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:02,020
And our sacred land
will sing again someday.

284
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,050
Someday.

285
00:18:05,133 --> 00:18:05,963
Someday, she must.

286
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,230
Huh?

287
00:18:18,313 --> 00:18:19,333
Is something happening?

288
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,457
Nothing you need worry about.

289
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:23,080
I've got a job to do.

290
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:24,456
You'll be safe here!

291
00:18:57,480 --> 00:18:58,520
He's right!

292
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:00,840
This pumpkin juice is fantastic!

293
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:05,940
Yes, he's quite good
at cultivating things.

294
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:20,850
Not the mast!

295
00:19:20,933 --> 00:19:21,940
Stop it, please!

296
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,820
Just stop burning the ship!

297
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:27,001
I'm serious, I don't want to die!

298
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:32,680
This is gonna hurt!

299
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:02,970
Oh, no.

300
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:06,010
Oh, no.

301
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,500
If you want me, that's fine.

302
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:10,017
But you can't have the ship.

303
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:12,837
They put me in charge of it,
and I'm not letting them down.

304
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,700
So you back off now, mister.

305
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:20,156
What do you think we should do, Vice?

306
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:21,660
He's so impassioned.

307
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:27,237
He doesn't want us to
hurt any of his friends.

308
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,657
He's begging us not to torch his ship!

309
00:20:29,740 --> 00:20:32,920
And he says, of course,
that he doesn't want to die.

310
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:35,180
I'm at a loss here?

311
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:38,497
You're a greedy little
hairball, aren't you?

312
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:40,120
And you get under my skin?

313
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:51,940
It's gone, Fall!

314
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:56,996
Why don't you try putting up a fight?

315
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:00,140
Your spear!

316
00:21:00,380 --> 00:21:02,204
It's burning through the metal!

317
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,060
Why is he burning everything?

318
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:15,160
You creep!

319
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:24,240
Are you trying to survive this without
sacrificing anything of yourself?

320
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:26,977
There's more to this guy
than he's showing me.

321
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:28,472
He's not just a fighter.

322
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:31,032
It's like he can predict all of my moves.

323
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:36,240
For one to live, another must die.

324
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:38,406
That is the way of the world.

325
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:41,000
This is a sacrificial altar.

326
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:46,760
What did you think was going
to happen by you being up here?

327
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:51,517
I was supposed to fix the ship and
wait until my crewmates came back.

328
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:55,417
Be assured your friends are trying
their hardest to get back here.

329
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:58,794
Of course they're going to
find it incredibly difficult.

330
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:01,700
On this island there are four areas,

331
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:04,764
each of which is governed
by a different priest.

332
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:09,120
Our first rule is that when
the targets are in one area,

333
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:13,379
the other priests are not supposed
to interfere with them in any way.

334
00:22:13,820 --> 00:22:18,780
But this sacrificial altar doesn't sit
inside the perimeter of any of the areas.

335
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:21,520
Here, we are in a freeze zone,

336
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:25,528
which means that any one of us
can attack those we find here.

337
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:28,497
And proper etiquette would
not have those at the altar

338
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:32,540
killed until after the targets
fail at a challenge and die.

339
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:34,310
What?!

340
00:22:34,393 --> 00:22:35,940
Luffy and the others are dead?!

341
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:37,520
Calm yourself.

342
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:40,337
The fact that I am here
does not necessarily

343
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:42,757
mean your friends are dead at this point.

344
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,680
It's unfortunate, but true.

345
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:48,800
I stand before you now with a
different purpose than sacrifice.

346
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:50,809
What's different about it?

347
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:52,190
Wait,

348
00:22:52,273 --> 00:22:54,617
you mean if my friends get
back here and rescue me,

349
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:57,937
then we're free to go, but you
won't let that happen, will you?

350
00:22:58,020 --> 00:23:00,080
Well, that depends on you.

351
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:04,737
And whether you and your crew can make
your escape from the Free Zone fast enough.

352
00:23:04,820 --> 00:23:05,650
What?

353
00:23:05,760 --> 00:23:07,200
But hold that thought.

354
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:12,681
The reason I'm here is because those are
the judgment rules under normal conditions.

355
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:13,790
However,

356
00:23:13,873 --> 00:23:18,349
when there is an exceptional situation,
the rules are set to change a little.

357
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:19,310
Exceptional?

358
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:21,780
Yes. Exceptional.

359
00:23:22,900 --> 00:23:24,057
Say, for example,

360
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:28,577
three sacrifices were to escape the altar
and swing to the main island using vines.

361
00:23:28,660 --> 00:23:30,700
Oh, that kind of situation.

362
00:23:31,900 --> 00:23:36,194
I say we should cross over and see
what's on the other side of the river.

363
00:23:45,220 --> 00:23:46,800
It's all hateful!

364
00:23:49,340 --> 00:23:54,046
Someone has to lose their life to bring
balance back after your friend's escape.

365
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:58,260
It's atonement, and
sacrifice is part of life.

366
00:23:58,660 --> 00:24:01,117
I want them to see it when they come back.

367
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:05,040
Their good friend lying on
deck, the life drained from him.

368
00:24:05,620 --> 00:24:09,000
Then they will realize the
severity of their mistakes.

369
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:15,040
And now, I offer your life to God!

370
00:24:18,020 --> 00:24:18,900
No!

371
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:29,080
Now die.

372
00:24:42,580 --> 00:24:44,277
Sorry to keep you waiting.

373
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:47,060
It's Gonfall, the skylight!

374
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:53,260
I wasn't expecting company.

375
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:02,390
Gonfall!

376
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:09,260
I knew you wouldn't let me down, skylight!

377
00:25:10,340 --> 00:25:12,777
We're not dealing with
an amateur here, Pierre.

378
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:17,213
I wouldn't want to disappoint a worthy
opponent with anything but our best

379
00:25:18,520 --> 00:25:21,897
What could that decrepit old
relic possibly be doing here?

380
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:24,451
Do you feel like putting him in his place?

381
00:25:26,620 --> 00:25:30,420
Enough stalling we don't
need two gods on this island

382
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:02,840
Oh, my God.

383
00:26:24,060 --> 00:26:27,600
Skye Knight, you're my hero! Help!

384
00:26:39,940 --> 00:26:44,440
One more hit in the right spot should
do it for him, eh, Pierre? Yeah!

385
00:26:50,420 --> 00:26:51,720
I've had enough!

386
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:56,857
You're nothing but a pathetic
shell of your former self.

387
00:26:56,940 --> 00:26:59,937
And I'm through playing games with a fool!

388
00:27:00,020 --> 00:27:02,717
You showed up to this fight a criminal.

389
00:27:02,800 --> 00:27:04,597
Which leaves me only one option.

390
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:06,180
Take you out.

391
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:10,580
Ordeal of string!

392
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:28,780
Ah-hoo!

393
00:27:29,220 --> 00:27:30,620
You're still alive!

394
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:31,780
I'm impressed!

395
00:27:32,100 --> 00:27:34,920
And as a reward for good behavior,

396
00:27:35,380 --> 00:27:37,557
we're going to finish our little fun today

397
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:41,000
with a move I've received
several awards for. Ah-hoo!

398
00:27:48,260 --> 00:27:50,520
My super-secret surprise!

399
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:20,780
Where have you been, child?

400
00:28:21,720 --> 00:28:22,550
Come a kitty!

401
00:28:22,780 --> 00:28:24,560
The upper yard again, right?

402
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:27,115
And that's probably Fourth in your bag.

403
00:28:28,580 --> 00:28:30,440
Stay away from that place, Isa.

404
00:28:32,260 --> 00:28:33,800
Or you will die.

405
00:28:36,600 --> 00:28:37,430
Nah!

406
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,986
You can't tell me what to do!

407
00:28:40,500 --> 00:28:43,240
You haven't even been
able to beat Inaru yet!

408
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:49,040
What a brat.

409
00:28:50,560 --> 00:28:51,390
What?

410
00:28:51,473 --> 00:28:52,600
An opportunity? That's right.

411
00:28:52,840 --> 00:28:55,217
For some reason, Gonfall
entered the upper yard,

412
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:57,617
which of course drew the
attention of the priests.

413
00:28:57,700 --> 00:28:58,530
You see,

414
00:28:58,613 --> 00:28:59,717
that old bag of bones thinks it's his

415
00:28:59,800 --> 00:29:02,624
responsibility to protect
the people of Skypiea.

416
00:29:03,060 --> 00:29:05,001
And that will only make him weak.

417
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:12,193
We would be wise to strike while our
enemies are occupied with each other.

418
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:19,180
The great warrior Kalgaras said,
light the fire of Shandora.

419
00:29:20,020 --> 00:29:22,000
Our people will do just that.

420
00:29:22,580 --> 00:29:24,500
No one can deny us our destiny,

421
00:29:24,700 --> 00:29:28,171
be it Gonfall or Eneru, and
now is the time to take action!

422
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:32,257
They have had the audacity to reign
as god, and that is unforgivable!

423
00:29:32,340 --> 00:29:35,037
No matter how different from
one another they may seem,

424
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:38,649
I assure you they are the same,
and they must be eliminated.

425
00:29:41,900 --> 00:29:42,730
Wiper,

426
00:29:42,813 --> 00:29:45,417
it has been six years
since Inneru began his

427
00:29:45,500 --> 00:29:48,117
reign and for the first
time since he took power.

428
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:50,437
A rebel has appeared on Angel Island.

429
00:29:50,520 --> 00:29:51,997
A young woman. I hear.

430
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:54,157
Get to the point, Locky.

431
00:29:54,240 --> 00:29:57,737
Because the Sky Knight rescued
the young rebel from judgment.

432
00:29:57,820 --> 00:30:01,037
Inneru now has reason to
directly confront Gonfall.

433
00:30:01,120 --> 00:30:02,177
In order to judge him,

434
00:30:02,260 --> 00:30:06,495
a battle like this between the former
god and the current god has never?

435
00:30:06,700 --> 00:30:10,347
happened, strategically this
could be most advantageous to us.

436
00:30:11,700 --> 00:30:15,120
We must remember that Gonfall
has never harmed any of us.

437
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:19,700
Not as the Sky Knight, and
not during his reign as God.

438
00:30:20,560 --> 00:30:22,837
The fact that he never
hurt any of us doesn't

439
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:25,777
change that he ruled with
absolute authority as God.

440
00:30:25,860 --> 00:30:29,978
And although he is our enemy's enemy,
that does not make him our ally.

441
00:30:30,140 --> 00:30:32,617
If he and one of the priests
kill each other in battle,

442
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:34,897
that will serve our purposes just fine.

443
00:30:34,980 --> 00:30:37,300
Otherwise, he is of no use to us.

444
00:30:40,120 --> 00:30:43,473
If you have any doubts at all
about this fight, stay out.

445
00:30:44,500 --> 00:30:46,029
You'll just be in the way.

446
00:30:50,620 --> 00:30:51,450
Ice.

447
00:30:53,300 --> 00:30:54,130
Upper Yard?

448
00:30:54,213 --> 00:30:55,043
What Upper Yard?

449
00:30:55,126 --> 00:30:57,561
I didn't go to Upper Yard,
I promise you I didn't!

450
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,620
You can't go into the tent yet.

451
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:05,737
Wiper descendant of the great
warrior Kokoro is angry right now.

452
00:31:05,820 --> 00:31:06,717
Careful.

453
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:12,157
Oh he's scary when he gets mad.

454
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:16,437
Scarier than God.

455
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:21,197
Help them?

456
00:31:21,280 --> 00:31:22,617
Us?

457
00:31:22,700 --> 00:31:26,517
How Conis?

458
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:27,637
My dear child?

459
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:29,317
It's only right.

460
00:31:29,400 --> 00:31:33,165
that you and I should try to
create some way for them to escape.

461
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:48,580
Wow, I can't believe how fast they are.

462
00:31:49,120 --> 00:31:49,950
Awesome.

463
00:31:52,060 --> 00:31:55,620
I can see that diplomacy is
no longer an option for me.

464
00:31:58,080 --> 00:31:59,609
Diplomacy is for the weak!

465
00:32:02,560 --> 00:32:04,260
This battle is intense.

466
00:32:12,340 --> 00:32:13,399
Heaven's judgment!

467
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:18,174
That young woman did something foolish.

468
00:32:19,960 --> 00:32:21,680
She brought this upon us.

469
00:32:22,380 --> 00:32:24,851
She knows we're not supposed to anger him.

470
00:32:45,020 --> 00:32:47,800
Please come back to us, God.

471
00:32:55,980 --> 00:32:57,500
You're mine.

472
00:33:02,600 --> 00:33:05,240
Is something wrong, Gonfall?

473
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:08,140
Shura, what have you done?

474
00:33:08,580 --> 00:33:10,920
Why can't we move?

475
00:33:11,540 --> 00:33:13,100
You old fool.

476
00:33:14,380 --> 00:33:16,220
Time to die.

477
00:33:30,080 --> 00:33:32,320
Mysterious, the strings are.

478
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:39,900
If you have the audacity to enter Upper
Yard, you must answer to the four priests.

479
00:33:40,220 --> 00:33:44,060
You were foolish to
think you could beat us.

480
00:33:44,400 --> 00:33:46,280
He's falling! Oh no!

481
00:33:48,500 --> 00:33:50,500
God Enuru is glorious.

482
00:33:51,800 --> 00:33:54,600
Perfect, and far beyond your reach.

483
00:34:00,040 --> 00:34:05,880
and our sacred land will sing
again someday someday she must

484
00:34:07,840 --> 00:34:08,670
Second!

485
00:34:08,753 --> 00:34:09,600
Second!
